<title>HUNGARY: AUSTRIA'S GANAHL TO INVEST ATS 60 MLN IN HUNGARY.</title>
<headline>AUSTRIA'S GANAHL TO INVEST ATS 60 MLN IN HUNGARY.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Austrian paper company Ganahl AG will invest 60 million Austrian shillings in its Hungarian subsidiary Rondo Kft to finance Rondo's purchase of a corrugated cardbord folding machine, Ganahl's CEO said.</p>
<p>The machinary will be placed in Rondo's Budapest factory, whose surface area will be increased to 14,300 square meters from 10,000 square meters to accommodate the equipment, Gunther Krametter told a news conference.</p>
<p>As a result of the investments, Rondo expects to be able to provide a more complete service to its customers, which include the Hungarian units of Philips, Coca-Cola and Nestle , he said.</p>
<p>Ganahl set up Rondo with a 250 million shilling investment in 1994. Rondo began producing cardboards the following year.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 40 40</p>
</text>
